00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:06.240
but I don't remember that day.

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:10.040
The memories my father shared 
with me of her, though,

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.580
are so strong I can still feel their warmth.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:17.590
Unless we care for these things ourselves,
 they won't be passed down.

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:22.270
Kiroranke Nispa showed me how 
many different people live.

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:26.830
Things I wouldn't have known 
if I'd stayed in Hokkaido.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:32.920
My journey through Karafuto was 
a journey to learn these things.

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:40.130
Were Kiroranke Nispa and Aca right? 
Do I have to fight to protect them?

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:45.870
You don't have to do it yourself, do you?

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:52.700
So are you telling me that once I find 
the gold, I need to go back to Otaru?

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:54.460
To spend my days chasing bear and deer,

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:56.750
and saying, "hinna, hinna" like 
I did when I met you?

00:19:57.460 --> 00:20:00.430
Kiroranke Nispa lost his life 
sharing these things with me.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:03.840
I'm a part of this now.

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:08.470
You still don't have to be the one that fights.

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:13.980
Sugimoto, aren't you trying to 
save yourself instead of me?

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:17.980
Aren't you just seeing in 
me the person you were

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:19.730
back when you ate dried persimmons?

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:29.620
That's part of it, yes.

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:37.540
I never told you what Wilk said just 
before he was shot at Abashiri.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:42.290
He told me that he'd raised you to 
hide in the mountains and fight.

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:46.510
To make you someone who could lead the Ainu.

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:54.170
Wilk got you caught up in this 
before you knew anything.

00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:59.690
And Kiroranke, even if he didn't 
mean to, put you in a position

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:04.740
where you'll feel like the only thing you can 
do is fight to protect what you care about.

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:07.780
I'll never forgive them for that.

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:10.890
"Become the leader of the Ainu and die."

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:13.500
"Fight and kill other people."

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:17.790
They basically put a curse on you!

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:21.570
I've never been a parent.

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:25.950
Maybe when you're a warrior and a parent, 
there's ways you can handle these things.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:29.260
But is that really what you want to do?

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:35.630
You told me that if you kill somebody, 
you go to some kind of hell, right?

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:40.520
You're not a religious girl. 
How do you interpret that?

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:46.900
Maybe the person who came up with the 
idea of hell was someone like me.

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:50.280
They killed a whole bunch of people and 
can't go back to who they were before.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:54.040
You're still lucky enough to 
not know what that's like.

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:58.980
I want you to leave the race for the gold.

00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:02.030
Because once you find out, it's too late.

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Sweet Lies</b>

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:39.230
Next time: "Sweet Lies"!
